{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://flightctl.local/contracts/v2/gpu-probe.schema.json",
  "title": "Flightctl GPU probe v2: inventory observation and occupancy observation",
  "description": "SPLIT (Grok finding 3/4): the single v1 GPUProbe.inspect returned two incompatible shapes. v2 has InventoryProbe (what cards exist) and OccupancyProbe (who is on the lane's cards now), each with the REAL nvidia-smi query it parses (x-real-commands; field names measured on driver 610.57.04 with nvidia-smi --help-query-gpu / --help-query-compute-apps, 2 Oct). Any failure, timeout, '[N/A]'-only row or unparsable output is status 'unknown' with a reason: never empty, never free.",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/inventory_observation"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/occupancy_observation"
    }
  ],
  "x-real-commands": {
    "inventory": "nvidia-smi --query-gpu=index,uuid,pci.bus_id,name,memory.total,driver_version --format=csv,noheader,nounits",
    "numa": "cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<pci_bus_id normalised>/numa_node",
    "occupancy_gpus": "nvidia-smi --query-gpu=uuid,memory.used,memory.total,utilization.gpu,temperature.gpu,power.draw,enforced.power.limit,clocks_event_reasons.hw_thermal_slowdown,clocks_event_reasons.sw_thermal_slowdown,ecc.errors.uncorrected.volatile.total --format=csv,noheader,nounits",
    "occupancy_processes": "nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=gpu_uuid,pid,process_name,used_memory --format=csv,noheader,nounits",
    "device_minor": "grep 'Device Minor' /proc/driver/nvidia/gpus/<pci_bus_id normalised>/information   (maps the card to /dev/nvidia<minor> for device-cgroup isolation; measured on driver 610.57.04, 2 Oct)",
    "notes": "Values may be '[N/A]' or '[Not Supported]' (ECC on Titan RTX reads '[N/A]', measured): map to null for that field, never to zero. clocks_event_reasons.* print 'Active'/'Not Active' (measured). pci.bus_id prints an 8-digit uppercase domain; normalise to 4-digit lowercase. process_name is the FULL command line on driver 610 (measured: a browser GPU process line of ~900 characters) and may contain ', ': parse a process row as uuid, pid = first two fields and used_memory = LAST field; everything between is the name. Compute-apps lists compute contexts only: graphics/display memory shows in memory.used with no process row (measured: 529 MiB used, zero process rows on a display-driving card). Every command runs with a bounded timeout (default 10 s). Amendment 5: values nvidia-smi does not print (a fractional or NaN integer field, a number outside the gpu_sample bounds, pid 0) make the observation unknown; a context type outside C, G, C+G is null.",
    "emptiness_rule": "Amendment 2 (Sol 6.1 cold review P1-1) replaces the size threshold. A lane is EMPTY only if: status ok; tenants empty; NO process attributed to the lease; the memory of noise processes sums to <= noise_cap_mib; and unexplained_mib < lane_noise_mib (graphics-only memory with no compute row). A process is NOISE only if its identity (owner uid, argv[0], context type G or C+G) matches the lane's noise_allowlist (noise_identity_ok); every other process is a TENANT whatever its size; unknown memory or identity is never noise. processes is PARTITIONED into lease / noise / external, and tenants == the external processes. occupancy_semantics() is the oracle; golden captures fix it. Rev 2: the context type is per (gpu_uuid, pid), never per pid.",
    "occupancy_process_types": "nvidia-smi -q -d PIDS -i <uuid>  (Amendment 5: the PER-CARD form, one call per lane card; plain `-q -d PIDS` keys its sections by PCI bus id, which the occupancy gpus query does not carry, measured. Per process: 'Type' C, G or C+G and 'Used GPU Memory'; measured 2 Oct on driver 610.57.04: a desktop browser GPU process holds a 5 MiB C+G context on a compute card, compositor/terminal contexts are G and do not appear in --query-compute-apps)",
    "process_identity": "stat /proc/<pid> (owner uid) and /proc/<pid>/cmdline (argv[0] = the text before the first NUL); unreadable = null = never noise. Amendment 5: an allow-list entry matches when argv0 EQUALS it or BEGINS with it followed by a space (argv0_matches), because some programs rewrite their command line into one string (measured: a browser GPU process, 817 and 912 bytes, one NUL) and executable paths may contain spaces (measured), so 'text before the first space' would be wrong. An argv0 that is empty or longer than 4096 characters is null (never noise), whatever an entry would match. /proc/<pid>/exe is not used: it is unreadable for another user's process (measured: readlink fails), and the probe runs as the executor account."
  },
  "$defs": {
    "status": {
      "enum": [
        "ok",
        "unknown"
      ]
    },
    "inventory_device": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "index",
        "uuid",
        "pci_bus_id",
        "name",
        "memory_total_mib",
        "driver_version",
        "numa_node",
        "device_minor"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "index": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "uuid": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^GPU-[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$"
        },
        "pci_bus_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{4}:[0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\\.[0-7]$"
        },
        "name": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1
        },
        "memory_total_mib": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1
        },
        "driver_version": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1
        },
        "numa_node": {
          "description": "From /sys/bus/pci/devices/<pci_bus_id>/numa_node. A sysfs value of -1 (no numa affinity reported) maps to null. Linux has at most 1024 nodes (MAX_NUMNODES = 1 << CONFIG_NODES_SHIFT, NODES_SHIFT at most 10), so a node id is 0-1023.",
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "maximum": 1023
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "device_minor": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "maximum": 255
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "/proc/driver/nvidia/gpus/<bus>/information 'Device Minor' -> /dev/nvidia<minor>; null = unknown (device isolation for the lane is then refused)."
        }
      }
    },
    "inventory_observation": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "kind",
        "host_id",
        "observed_at",
        "status",
        "reason",
        "vendor",
        "devices"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "const": "gpu-inventory"
        },
        "host_id": {
          "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/short_identifier"
        },
        "observed_at": {
          "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/utc_time"
        },
        "status": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/status"
        },
        "reason": {
          "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/nullable_text"
        },
        "vendor": {
          "enum": [
            "nvidia",
            "none",
            "unknown"
          ]
        },
        "devices": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/inventory_device"
          }
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "unknown"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "reason": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "devices": {
                "maxItems": 0
              },
              "vendor": {
                "const": "unknown"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "vendor": {
                "const": "none"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "ok"
              },
              "devices": {
                "maxItems": 0
              },
              "reason": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "gpu_sample": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "uuid",
        "memory_used_mib",
        "memory_total_mib",
        "utilization_pct",
        "temperature_c",
        "power_draw_w",
        "power_limit_w",
        "thermal_slowdown",
        "ecc_uncorrected"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "uuid": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/inventory_device/properties/uuid"
        },
        "memory_used_mib": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "memory_total_mib": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1
        },
        "utilization_pct": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "maximum": 100
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "temperature_c": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "maximum": 130
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "power_draw_w": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "power_limit_w": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "thermal_slowdown": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "ecc_uncorrected": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "gpu_process": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "gpu_uuid",
        "pid",
        "process_name",
        "used_memory_mib",
        "attribution",
        "uid",
        "argv0",
        "context_type"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "gpu_uuid": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/inventory_device/properties/uuid"
        },
        "pid": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1
        },
        "process_name": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 4096
        },
        "used_memory_mib": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "attribution": {
          "description": "Set by the executor, not the probe: lease (inside the lease's unit cgroup or a registered holder pid), noise (an allow-listed desktop identity: noise_identity_ok, Amendment 2), external (anything else, WHATEVER its size). Amendment 3 rev 2 (Sol 6.1 amd3 P1-4): a friend session's processes (a CUDA child in user-<uid>.slice) are 'lease' ONLY when the process's cgroup path lies inside the user slice that an OPEN entry of the executor's session registry records for THIS lane (the entry exists only after the helper's session-open succeeded for that parent lease); the parent is that entry's parent_lease_id. The uid is never used: a friend-uid process outside a registered slice, or inside the slice of a closed or other-lane entry, is 'external'. Oracle session_attribution.",
          "enum": [
            "unattributed",
            "lease",
            "noise",
            "external"
          ]
        },
        "uid": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Owner uid of /proc/<pid> (null = not readable: then never noise)."
        },
        "argv0": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 4096
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "argv[0] from /proc/<pid>/cmdline: the text before the first NUL (null = not readable). Amendment 5: matched against an allow-list entry by equality or by the entry followed by a space (argv0_matches)."
        },
        "context_type": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "enum": [
                "C",
                "G",
                "C+G"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "nvidia-smi -q -d PIDS 'Type' (measured 2 Oct, driver 610.57.04: C, G, C+G). A pure compute 'C' context is never noise. Rev 2 (Sol 6.1 amd2): taken per DEVICE ENTRY (gpu_uuid, pid); the same pid can be C+G on one card and C on another."
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "attribution": {
                "const": "noise"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "used_memory_mib": {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "uid": {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "argv0": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "context_type": {
                "enum": [
                  "G",
                  "C+G"
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "occupancy_observation": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "kind",
        "host_id",
        "lane_id",
        "observed_at",
        "status",
        "reason",
        "expected_uuids",
        "gpus",
        "processes",
        "tenants",
        "noise",
        "lane_memory_used_mib",
        "thresholds",
        "unexplained_mib",
        "empty"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "const": "gpu-occupancy"
        },
        "host_id": {
          "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/short_identifier"
        },
        "lane_id": {
          "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/short_identifier"
        },
        "observed_at": {
          "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/utc_time"
        },
        "status": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/status"
        },
        "reason": {
          "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/nullable_text"
        },
        "gpus": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/gpu_sample"
          },
          "description": "One sample per expected lane card (status ok)."
        },
        "processes": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/gpu_process"
          }
        },
        "tenants": {
          "description": "Amendment 2: every process that is neither attributed to the lease nor an allow-listed desktop identity, WHATEVER its memory (a ~300 MiB stray CUDA context is a tenant: T10). Unknown memory or identity is never noise.",
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/gpu_process"
          }
        },
        "noise": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/gpu_process"
          }
        },
        "lane_memory_used_mib": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "thresholds": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "lane_noise_mib",
            "noise_cap_mib",
            "noise_allowlist"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "lane_noise_mib": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            "noise_cap_mib": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "description": "Amendment 2: aggregate cap on the memory of allow-listed noise processes on the lane; above it the lane is not empty."
            },
            "noise_allowlist": {
              "type": "array",
              "uniqueItems": true,
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "required": [
                  "argv0",
                  "uid"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "argv0": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "maxLength": 4096,
                    "pattern": "^[^ \\t-\\r]([\\s\\S]*[^ \\t-\\r])?(?![\\s\\S])",
                    "description": "Amendment 10: no leading or trailing ASCII whitespace (U+0020, U+0009-U+000D); whitespace inside stays legal. The end anchor is (?![\\s\\S]), not $, because Python's $ also matches before a final newline."
                  },
                  "uid": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1
                  }
                }
              },
              "description": "Amendment 2: approved desktop/display identities for this lane: argv[0] of /proc/<pid>/cmdline AND the owner uid of /proc/<pid>. An entry trusts that uid (argv[0] is forgeable only by its own processes); root and DynamicUser uids are never noise. Empty = nothing is noise."
            }
          }
        },
        "unexplained_mib": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Sum of memory.used over the lane's cards minus memory of lease-attributed and noise processes; null when status is unknown."
        },
        "empty": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "The ONLY GPU-empty proof (x-real-commands.emptiness_rule). Consistency with the numbers is checked by occupancy_semantics()."
        },
        "expected_uuids": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "uniqueItems": true,
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/inventory_device/properties/uuid"
          },
          "description": "Round 4 (Sol 6 r3 B2): the lane's card UUIDs from the confirmed inventory. With status ok, gpus must cover exactly these (all present, none extra, no duplicates) and every process must be on one of them; occupancy_semantics() enforces it."
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "unknown"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "reason": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "tenants": {
                "maxItems": 0
              },
              "gpus": {
                "maxItems": 0
              },
              "empty": {
                "const": false
              },
              "unexplained_mib": {
                "type": "null"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "ok"
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "gpus": {
                "minItems": 1
              },
              "unexplained_mib": {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "lane_memory_used_mib": {
                "type": "integer"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "empty": {
                "const": true
              }
            }
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "ok"
              },
              "tenants": {
                "maxItems": 0
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
